Original commit body from fac14b66de8dc4187761cc8d219fdb4446f1ef9a:

perl.py's method_call_expression arm looked a method on an EXPRESSION
invocant ($obj->m, shift->m, Pkg->new->m) up by short name across every
package, so a repo sub named `get` captured HTTP::Tiny->new->get($u),
and emitted nothing outside a sub.

The invocant is now typed where the file states it: Pkg->new (only
`new` constructs; DBI->connect returns a handle), a scalar assigned
one, and the method invocant -- $self/$this/$class taken by shift or as
the first of @_, or a bare shift->m outside main -- as the enclosing
package. A typed call resolves like a class-method call with
call_construct=method; an untyped one gets the honest
perl:external:0-0:<m>:unresolved method edge (WI-johib's rule). Top-level
calls are attributed to the file.

The invocant is typed by NAME: typing by shape (any first shift / @_)
was measured to type a plain function's first argument, a second shift
and a $SIG{__DIE__} handler's argument as the enclosing package
(postgresql: 311 edges moved onto the wrong package; 5 after).

Measured against dev (frozen corpus, perl files): resolved calls
postgresql +7,363 / -581, virtualbox +959 / -744, git +34 / -173. The
removed edges are receiver-blind binds; 554 / 551 / 122 of them are now
external method edges. A 15-edge sample of the new resolutions was all
correct. Two tests pinned the old short-name binding (test_perl's
method-call test, test_perl_class_method's out-of-scope pin) and now
assert the typed / unresolved result.

